      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>No line-break word style is specified. When <see cref="M:Android.Graphics.Text.LineBreakConfig.Builder.Merge(Android.Graphics.Text.LineBreakConfig)" /> merges a configuration with an unspecified word style, it keeps the builder's existing word style.</para>
          <code lang="text/java">    LineBreakConfig override = new LineBreakConfig.Builder()
         .setLineBreakStyle(LineBreakConfig.LINE_BREAK_STYLE_STRICT)
         .build();  // UNSPECIFIED if no setLineBreakWordStyle is called.
    LineBreakConfig config = new LineBreakConfig.Builder()
         .setLineBreakWordStyle(LineBreakConfig.LINE_BREAK_WORD_STYLE_PHRASE)
         .merge(override)
         .build();
    // Here, config has LINE_BREAK_STYLE_STRICT for line break config and
    // LINE_BREAK_WORD_STYLE_PHRASE for line break word style.</code>
          <para>For text layout, this value resolves to <see cref="F:Android.Graphics.Text.LineBreakWordStyle.None" /> when the target SDK is API level 34 or earlier, and to <see cref="F:Android.Graphics.Text.LineBreakWordStyle.Auto" /> when the target SDK is API level 35 or later.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/text/LineBreakConfig#LINE_BREAK_WORD_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.graphics.text.LineBreakConfig.LINE_BREAK_WORD_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED</code>.</a></format></para>
